  "notes": "すてき is a na-adjective expressing genuine admiration for something wonderful or lovely.\n\nKANJI:\nCan be written as {素敵|すてき} but hiragana is common.\n\nFORMS:\n- すてきな + noun: a lovely ~\n- すてきに: wonderfully (adverbial)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- すてきな{服|ふく}: lovely clothes\n- すてきな{考|かんが}え: wonderful idea\n- すてきな{人|ひと}: lovely person\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\nOften used by women; expresses genuine positive admiration.\n\nSIMILAR:\n- {素晴|すば}らしい: wonderful (more emphatic)\n- きれい: beautiful, pretty",
